course: dictionary
lesson: 2807
title: Dissolve: when things mix in and disappear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To dissolve means to mix into a liquid so completely that you can no longer see it. Stir a spoon of sugar into your tea and it dissolves. Dissolve is a verb, so it changes its form: dissolves, dissolved, dissolving.
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. «Salt is spread on icy roads because the salt dissolves in the thin wet layer on the ice.» The salt disappears into the water, so dissolve must mean mix in completely and vanish from sight.
explain: Dissolve has other meanings too. «To dissolve a group» means to end it officially, and «she dissolved into tears» means she started crying uncontrollably. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Dissolve means to mix into a liquid so completely that you cannot see it any more.
fact: A solid that dissolves is soluble, like salt or sugar. A solid that does not dissolve is insoluble, like sand or chalk.
fact: The mixture made when a solid dissolves in a liquid is called a solution.
fact: Warm water and stirring help things dissolve faster.
fact: Sand does not dissolve in water, because its particles are joined too strongly for water to pull them apart.
exercise: «Sugar dissolves in tea when you stir it.» What does dissolves mean here? | Floats on top in lumps | Sinks to the bottom in one piece | *Mixes in completely so you cannot see it | Goes hard and stays still
exercise: What is the word for a solid that does not dissolve in water, like sand or chalk? | Dissolving | Solution | *Insoluble | Soluble
exercise: Find and copy the word for the mixture made when a solid dissolves in a liquid. | sand | sugar | stirred | *solution
test: «To dissolve a group» means what? | Make it bigger | Stir it round | *End it officially | Start it up
test: «She dissolved into tears when she heard the news.» What does dissolved into tears mean? | *Began crying uncontrollably | Ate a sweet | Mixed into water | Forgot the news
exam: Why does sand not dissolve in water? | Because sand is a liquid | *Because its particles are joined too strongly for water to pull them apart | Because water is too cold for it | Because sand is too heavy to move
